    body: '다음 글의 목적으로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Dear Library Members,<br>For many years, Westbrook Public Library has charged a small fee for every day a book is returned late. We introduced this rule to encourage members to bring books back on time, but our records tell a different story. The fees have not made returns noticeably faster. Instead, they have kept some people, especially children and families with tight budgets, from visiting the library at all, because they are embarrassed about unpaid charges. We believe that a library should open doors, not close them. Therefore, starting on March 1, we will no longer charge fees for overdue books, and all existing late charges on members’ accounts will be cleared. We still ask you to return books when they are due so that others can enjoy them. We look forward to welcoming back familiar faces.<br>Warm regards,<br>Helen Brooks, Library Director</div>',
