    body: '밑줄 친 <u>watering the weeds</u>가 다음 글에서 의미하는 바로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">A teacher who wants to improve her students’ behavior often begins by pointing out what is going wrong. She stops the class to scold the boy who is talking, reminds the girl who forgot her homework, and comments on every interruption. Yet the problems frequently grow worse rather than better. For some students, attention of any kind is a reward, and being corrected in front of everyone is far more noticeable than quietly doing the right thing. Meanwhile, the students who are working hard receive no attention at all. A gardener who carefully waters only the weeds should not be surprised when they take over the garden. A more effective approach is to notice and name the behavior you want to see: thanking the student who helped a classmate, or praising the group that started work quickly. When we keep <u>watering the weeds</u>, we feed the very behavior we are trying to remove.</div>',
