    slot: '제목',
    body: '다음 글의 제목으로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">After a test is returned, most students look at their score and put the paper away as quickly as possible. The wrong answers are an unpleasant reminder of failure, so they are quickly forgotten. Yet those wrong answers contain the most useful information the test can offer. A correct answer tells you little, since you might have known the material or simply guessed well. A wrong answer, on the other hand, points directly to something you have misunderstood. If you look closely, you may discover a pattern: perhaps you keep misreading questions, confuse two similar ideas, or run out of time on the last section. Each of these problems has a different solution, and you can only find it by studying your mistakes. Ten minutes spent analyzing errors is often worth more than an hour spent reviewing material you already know. A wrong answer is not the end of learning but a sign showing where to go next.</div>',
