    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">It is tempting to think that a scientific theory is overturned the moment it meets a contradicting observation. The history of science suggests otherwise. When astronomers noticed that the orbit of Uranus did not match the predictions of Newtonian mechanics, they did not abandon Newton. Instead, they proposed that an unseen planet was pulling on Uranus, and the discovery of Neptune proved them right. Not long afterward, a similar irregularity in the orbit of Mercury led to a search for another hidden planet, which was never found; the puzzle was resolved only by Einstein’s general relativity. In both cases, scientists responded to the anomaly in the same reasonable way, yet one response rescued the old theory while the other merely postponed its replacement. What this shows is that an anomaly does not, by itself, tell scientists ________. Whether it signals a flaw in the theory or a gap in our knowledge of the world can often be judged only in hindsight.</div>',
