    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Engineers who design a system for maximum efficiency typically strip away anything that does not contribute directly to its function. Living organisms, shaped by evolution rather than design, rarely look so tidy. Many genes have near-duplicates that perform overlapping roles, so that disabling one often produces no visible effect at all. To an efficiency-minded observer, this looks like waste: why maintain two copies of a tool when one would do? The answer becomes clear when conditions change. Genes that seem dispensable in the comfortable conditions of a laboratory often prove vital when an organism faces heat, starvation, or infection. An organism whose every component is essential can be brought down by a single mutation or a single unusual stress, while one that carries spare capacity can absorb the damage and carry on. Over the long history of life, environments have shifted far too often for the leanest designs to prevail. What appears inefficient at any given moment, in other words, may be ________.</div>',
    type: 'choice',
    choices: [
      'a sign that evolution has stopped working',
      'a mistake that engineers can easily correct',
      'the reason organisms age and eventually die',
      'the price of surviving an unpredictable future',
      'evidence that genes compete with one another',
    ],
    answer: 4,
    concepts: ['e-blank'],
    hint: '‘The answer becomes clear when conditions change.’ 낭비처럼 보이는 여분이 언제 쓸모 있었나요?',
    solution:
      '<ol class="sol-steps"><li>핵심 문장: <i>one that carries spare capacity can absorb the damage and carry on.</i> → 여분을 가진 생물은 손상을 견디고 살아남는다.</li><li><i>environments have shifted far too often for the leanest designs to prevail.</i> → 환경이 너무 자주 바뀌어서 가장 군더더기 없는 설계는 살아남지 못했다.</li><li>→ 지금 비효율로 보이는 것은 <b>예측할 수 없는 미래를 견디기 위한 대가</b>일 수 있다 → ④</li><li>① 진화가 멈춘 신호: 오히려 진화가 만든 결과예요. ② 엔지니어가 쉽게 고칠 실수: 글은 그것이 실수가 아니라고 해요. ③ 노화와 죽음의 원인: 근거 없음. ⑤ 유전자끼리 경쟁: 중복 유전자는 ‘겹치는 역할’을 할 뿐 경쟁 이야기는 없어요.</li></ol><div class="sol-ans">답: <b>④</b></div><div class="sol-warn"><b>많이 틀리는 곳</b> 첫 문장의 엔지니어 이야기에 끌려 ②를 고르기 쉬워요. 엔지니어는 <b>대비를 위해 꺼낸 비교 대상</b>일 뿐이고, 글은 그들의 효율 기준이 생물에는 맞지 않는다고 말해요.</div>',
    mistakes: ['② 고르기: 엔지니어 관점을 글쓴이 관점으로 착각', 'in other words가 앞 문장(환경 변화)을 다시 말한다는 걸 놓침'],
