    body: '주어진 글 다음에 이어질 글의 순서로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">During a recession, it seems only sensible for a family to cut spending and save more for an uncertain future. Spending less on restaurants, vacations, and new cars, and putting the money aside, looks like the responsible thing to do.</div><div class="passage">(A) The resulting fall in incomes leaves households less able to save than before. Thus, the effort to save more can end up reducing the total amount saved — a result economists call the paradox of thrift.<br>(B) For any single household, this is indeed a wise decision, since savings protect it against a lost job or an unexpected bill. The problem arises when millions of households make the same choice at the same time.<br>(C) One family’s spending is another family’s income. When everyone spends less, businesses sell less, and they respond by reducing wages or cutting jobs. Those workers, now earning less or nothing at all, cut their own spending in turn.</div>',
