    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Psychologists call this the spotlight effect, and they trace it to a simple asymmetry.</div><div class="passage">( ① ) People who make a social blunder, such as wearing an embarrassing shirt, typically assume that everyone around them has noticed, and they replay the moment in their minds for hours afterward. ( ② ) In one experiment, students were asked to wear a T-shirt printed with the face of an unfashionable singer into a room full of peers. ( ③ ) Afterward, they estimated that about half of the people present had noticed the shirt. ( ④ ) In fact, only about a quarter had. ( ⑤ ) Because we experience our own appearance and actions so vividly, we wrongly assume that others are paying them the same attention. We forget that others are just as absorbed in their own appearance and worries as we are in ours. The lesson is reassuring: most of our minor embarrassments pass largely unseen.</div>',
