    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">The reasoning breaks down, however, once people begin to rely on the crowd instead of on their own judgment.</div><div class="passage">( ① ) Imagine choosing between two unfamiliar restaurants on a street, one crowded and one empty. ( ② ) Most people pick the crowded one, reasoning that the diners there must know something they do not, perhaps about the food or the prices. ( ③ ) This is often sensible, since the choices of others do carry information. ( ④ ) Suppose that the first few diners simply chose at random, and each later arrival, seeing a crowd, followed along. ( ⑤ ) The crowd would then grow ever larger while containing no more information than the guesses of the first few customers. Economists call this an information cascade, a pattern in which a crowd’s size reflects imitation rather than knowledge. Such cascades help explain why fashions and even investment bubbles can grow rapidly on remarkably thin foundations.</div>',
