    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Medieval European maps often placed Jerusalem at the center of the world, while many Chinese maps placed China there.</div><div class="passage">( ① ) Such choices were not errors of measurement but statements about what mattered. ( ② ) A map, after all, cannot show everything; it must decide what to include, what to enlarge, and what to place at its heart. ( ③ ) Modern maps may seem free of such judgments, since they are based on satellite data and precise surveys rather than on religious or political beliefs. ( ④ ) Yet even they must choose a projection, and every projection distorts size or shape somewhere on the globe. ( ⑤ ) The familiar Mercator map, for example, makes Greenland appear nearly as large as Africa, which is in reality about fourteen times larger. The choice of projection, like the choice of a center, quietly shapes how viewers imagine the relative importance of the world’s regions.</div>',
