    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">When a change is timed to coincide with such an interruption, even a large one can go unnoticed.</div><div class="passage">We feel as though we see the whole scene in front of us in rich detail. ( ① ) In fact, at any moment we take in fine detail only from a small region at the center of our gaze, and much of the rest is filled in by expectation. ( ② ) This usually works well, because a change in the world normally produces a flicker of motion that automatically pulls our attention toward it. ( ③ ) That signal can be hidden, though, by a blink, a quick eye movement, or a cut in a film — interruptions so frequent that we hardly notice them. ( ④ ) Viewers have failed to notice a building vanishing from the background of a photograph, or an actor’s shirt changing color between shots. ( ⑤ ) Such failures suggest that our sense of seeing everything is less a record of the world than a confident assumption that the world has stayed the same.</div>',
