    slot: '문장 삽입 · 고난도',
    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">In such a conversation, the fast speaker, uncomfortable with the silence, jumps in before the other has finished thinking; the slow speaker, waiting for a polite opening, never finds one.</div><div class="passage">In conversation, a pause is never simply empty. ( ① ) Listeners read meaning into it, and what they read depends on what they are used to. ( ② ) In some communities, a gap of a second or two before answering signals that the listener is taking the question seriously and giving it thought. ( ③ ) In others, the same gap suggests hesitation, disagreement, or even dishonesty, and speakers rush to fill it. ( ④ ) Trouble arises when people from these two backgrounds talk with each other. ( ⑤ ) As a result, each misjudges the other without realizing why: the slower speaker finds the faster one pushy and inattentive, while the faster speaker finds the slower one evasive or unfriendly. Neither is aware that the problem lies not in what was said but in the spaces between.</div>',
