    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Careful measurement shows that at room temperature the flow of glass would be far too slow to produce any visible change, even over the entire age of the universe.</div><div class="passage">Visitors to old European churches are sometimes told that the windows are thicker at the bottom because glass is really a liquid that flows, very slowly, downward over the centuries. ( ① ) The story is appealing, and it seems to fit what one sees: many medieval panes are indeed uneven, with one edge heavier than the other. ( ② ) It also draws on a real feature of glass, which, unlike a typical solid, lacks a regular crystal structure, so that its atoms are arranged as irregularly as those of a liquid. ( ③ ) Nonetheless, having the structure of a liquid is not the same as behaving like one. ( ④ ) The real explanation for the uneven panes lies in how they were made. ( ⑤ ) Early glassmakers spun molten glass into large disks that were never perfectly even, and when the disks were cut into panes, workers often set the heavier edge at the bottom, where it seemed more stable; indeed, panes are occasionally found installed thick side up.</div>',
